# Box-size calibration (NM amplitude model)

Turns the NM-helper box into an actual prediction: the NM amplitude is
predicted from cheap structure/NMA descriptors, calibrated on MD data, and
tested on held-out proteins. The MD box of a protein is never used to build
that protein's box.

```text
calib_required_box.py   per protein   MD replicas -> per-frame extents (how much room it needed)
calib_nm_envelope.py    per protein   NM helpers  -> box extent vs amplitude, NMA descriptors
calib_fit_model.py      all proteins  amplitude model + held-out evaluation vs standard boxes
calib_geometry.py       shared NumPy geometry (unwrapping, superposition, envelopes)
test_calib.py           self-tests on synthetic data (no MDTraj/R needed)
calib_slurm_example.sh  SLURM array for the per-protein steps
```

Definitions

* Extent along axis a: max minus min heavy-atom coordinate. A rectangular box
  with side L_a keeps periodic images at least c apart along a when
  L_a >= extent_a + c.
* Required extent: max over all MD frames (all replicas). `lab` keeps the
  protein's tumbling (plain MD); `body` removes rotation (flexibility only).
* Amplitude A: RMS per-atom displacement (nm) along each of the first K
  internal modes (Bio3D 7..6+K). `thermal` scaling gives mode m
  A*sqrt(lambda_7/lambda_m).
* A*: smallest A for which the NM envelope covers the required extent on all
  three axes.
* Model: conformalised linear quantile regression of log(A*) on descriptors
  (size, shape, terminal coil, NMA flexibility), feature set chosen by
  repeated CV on the training proteins only.

Run

```bash
python test_calib.py                                    # sanity check
sbatch --array=1-N%20 calib_slurm_example.sh            # steps 1+2 per protein
python calib_fit_model.py --pdb-list passing_pdbs.txt \
    --frame lab --stat max --scaling thermal --n-modes 10 \
    --cutoff 1.2 --standard-d 1.0 --quantile 0.95
```

Results go to `results/calibration/<tag>/`: `summary.json` (held-out
coverage and box volume relative to the standard cubic box, per method),
`model.json` (coefficients), `test_predictions.csv`, `feature_search_cv.csv`
and plots.

Known limitations

* The NM envelope does not model rotation. With `--frame lab` the amplitude
  absorbs tumbling, so the calibration is specific to the simulation length
  used; with `--frame body` the boxes are only safe if rotation is restrained.
* Rectangular boxes only; dodecahedral boxes need a rotation-invariant
  criterion.
* Uses Bio3D `U`; check whether mass-weighting makes `modes` the right choice.

